window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"rumble","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 3","text":"Electro Harpoon slows peel him off you — but Overheat lockouts keep the stage honest at 3."},{"when":"Danger Zone windows","text":"Empowered Q is your best damage; time it to his Ashen Pursuit, not to your own panic."},{"when":"Locke first item","text":"Purgatory executes you out of a telegraphed Equalizer channel from 1000 range — his one clear window."},{"when":"Two items","text":"Scrap Shield answers his burst and the fight returns to a fair, repeatable coinflip."}],"wants":{"you":["Heat managed to Danger Zone on his blink-in","Harpoon slows before he closes","Equalizer fired only above his floor"],"foe":["You Overheated with every cast locked","A low-HP target for the Purgatory execute","You channeling R inside his 1000"]},"early":"The laning phase is a heat-management coinflip: your Q damage is real but heat-gated, and Silver Stake scales with the health you have lost, so every point you drop makes his autos hit harder. Trade in Danger Zone windows, harpoon him off you at 3, and never Overheat while Ashen Pursuit is up.","mid":"At 6 the stage stays even — empowered Q trades match his all-in — but his first item plus Purgatory (120s) is the one clear tilt: it is a 1000-range throw that executes, so it reaches you inside a telegraphed Equalizer channel. Never fire R at low HP in his line, and stay above the floor.","late":"Post-items it evens back out: Scrap Shield answers his burst and the fight becomes repeatable. Soul Ignition (18s) costs him his own health and refunds only part of it at the END of the duration — Grievous Wounds applied before that tick denies the refund entirely. Zone with Equalizer from angles he cannot reach.","whys":["Level 1 is even: your heat-gated Q offsets Silver Stake, which grows with the health you have lost.","At 2 the trades stay skill-based, hinging on your heat bar and whether Ritual Nails actually lands.","At 3 your harpoon slows peel him, but Overheat lockout keeps the stage honest and even.","Through 4-5 it is heat management against a flat 10-second Ashen Pursuit — still even.","At 6 it stays even: empowered Q trades answer Purgatory while you hold above the floor.","With his first item, Purgatory executes you out of a telegraphed Equalizer channel from 1000 range — his stage.","Post-items it evens again: Scrap Shield answers his burst in a fair, repeatable fight."]});
