window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"rumble","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Rumble","Rumble","Skill","Zaahen","Skill","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 2","text":"Flamespitter shoves him off the wave — but Dreaded Return pulls you in from 850 units."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"Double harpoon slows beat his walk-up, but not Aureate Rush — a 10s dash at rank 1."},{"when":"Your first item","text":"Your AP spike answers his sustain — but only Grievous Wounds stops Q and R healing."},{"when":"Two items","text":"Cultivation of War banks AD all fight and can revive him — never brawl long."}],"wants":{"you":["Flamespitter him before Aureate Rush lands","Heat up for the Dreaded Return","Equalizer slowing his Aureate Rush path"],"foe":["Determination stacked before he commits","Grim Deliverance landing while Q is down","Long brawls where Q and R heal him back"]},"early":"After an even level 1 the lane is yours: level-2 Flamespitter shoves him off the wave and by 3 your cone plus double harpoon own the spacing. His gap-close is not weak — Aureate Rush is a 10-second dash and Dreaded Return pulls you in from 850, the range you harpoon from. Trade once he has spent one.","mid":"At 6 treat it as even: your Equalizer forces his engages wide, but his R all-in can still flip any fight where you overheat or mis-slot the wall, so place it early and honestly. Your first-item AP spike restores clear control — poke and kite out-damage his sustain and he cannot force you to stand still.","late":"Late you do not dictate the sidelane. Cultivation of War banks bonus AD off every attack he lands on you, and at full Determination he revives, so a long brawl ends his way even when you were winning it. Kite with harpoon, spend Equalizer on where the teamfight happens, and never take the flame duel at low heat.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you have no heat built yet, so there is nothing to zone him with.","At 2 Flamespitter pushes him off the wave; The Darkin Glaive resets his auto — read the wind-up.","By 3 your cone plus double harpoon own the spacing, but Aureate Rush is a 10s dash in.","Levels 4-5 read even — Dreaded Return is 14s at rank 1, so trade once he has spent it.","At 6 Grim Deliverance is a 110s all-in that heals him through your cone — his stage, not yours.","Your first-item AP spike matches his sustain, but only with Grievous Wounds bought — call it even.","Late Cultivation of War banks AD through every fight and can revive him — refuse the sidelane."]});
